>
>But they are all heavier, right?  This was discussed recently by people
>far more experienced than me, so I've taken it as gospel.  

They do provide less nutrition per unit weight than royal jelly, yes.
However, I've never had any trouble fitting enough K-rations for the
endgame into my bag of holding.

K-rations are plentiful, consumable in a single turn, and high in
nutrition, which makes them the most *practical* choice for your endgame
food.  Royal jelly has special effects which mean that it's often
profitable to just eat it all as fast as you safely can.

I've had plenty of games where the only beehive is the one in Rodney's
tower; I've never had a winning game that wasn't reasonably richly endowed
with randomly generated sergeants and soldiers.
